/-!
# Derived completeness on `X_proét` and restriction to a locally closed subscheme

Let `X` be a scheme, `Λ` a Noetherian ring and `I ⊆ Λ` an ideal. For an object `K` of
`D(X_proét, Λ)` the two senses of derived completeness — along the ideal sheaf `I·\underline{Λ}`
of the ringed site (Stacks 0999), and along `I` for the `Λ`-linear derived category of sheaves
of `Λ`-modules (Stacks 091S) — agree. One implication is
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.isDerivedComplete_derivedModuleEquiv_inverse_obj`; the converse is
proved here. Derived completeness along the ideal sheaf is tested on derived sections over the
affine objects with w-contractible ring of global sections `W`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_iff_derivedSections_of_sliceTestingFamily`); there
the sections of `I·\underline{Λ}` form the ideal generated by `I` in `Γ(W, \underline{Λ})`, the
scalars at which a complex is derived complete form an ideal, and derived sections over `W` carry
multiplication by `l ∈ Λ` to multiplication by its image in `Γ(W, \underline{Λ})` and preserve
countable products.

The second sense is the one inverse image visibly preserves along an immersion `g : Z ⟶ X`:
`g⁻¹` is exact and `Λ`-linear, and it commutes with countable products (Stacks 09BU), which are
exact on both sides; so `g⁻¹` carries `T(K, l) = 0` to `T(g⁻¹K, l) = 0`. Hence restriction of a
derived complete object of `D(X_proét, Λ)` to a locally closed subscheme is derived complete.

## Main results

* `ProEtale.isDerivedComplete_of_isDerivedComplete_derivedModuleEquiv_inverse_obj`:
  derived completeness along `I` gives derived completeness along `I·\underline{Λ}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.isDerivedComplete_derivedInverseImage`: restriction along an
  immersion preserves derived completeness.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.isConstructibleDerivedSheaf_derivedInverseImage`: restriction of an
  object of `D_cons(X, Λ)`, `X` quasi-compact, to a locally closed subscheme on which the reduction
  has locally constant cohomology of finite type lies in `D_cons`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0999](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0999)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 091S](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/091S)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09BU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09BU)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite
open scoped IsMulCommutative

universe u w

/-- **A left adjoint of a functor commuting with multiplication by scalars commutes with it too.**
If the right adjoint `G` carries `r • 𝟙` to `r • 𝟙`, so does the left adjoint `L`: both sides
correspond under the adjunction to `(r • 𝟙) ≫ η`. -/
theorem CategoryTheory.Adjunction.map_smul_id_of_map_smul_id {R : Type*} [Semiring R]
    {C D : Type*} [Category* C] [Category* D] [Preadditive C] [Preadditive D] [Linear R C]
    [Linear R D] {L : C ⥤ D} {G : D ⥤ C} (adj : L ⊣ G)
    (hG : ∀ (Y : D) (r : R), G.map (r • 𝟙 Y) = r • 𝟙 (G.obj Y)) (X : C) (r : R) :
    L.map (r • 𝟙 X) = r • 𝟙 (L.obj X) := by
  refine (adj.homEquiv _ _).injective ?_
  rw [Adjunction.homEquiv_unit, Adjunction.homEquiv_unit, hG, Linear.comp_smul]
  refine (adj.unit.naturality (r • 𝟙 X)).symm.trans ?_
  simp

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard
  SheafOfModules.hasSheafify_commRingCat
  Stacks.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_commRingCat
  SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_commRingCat
  GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat
  SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat

variable (X : Scheme.{u}) {Λ : Type (max (u + 1) w)} [CommRing Λ] [IsNoetherianRing Λ]

/-- **Derived completeness along `I` gives derived completeness along `I·\underline{Λ}`.** If the
complex of sheaves of `Λ`-modules corresponding to an object `K` of `D(X_proét, Λ)` is derived
complete along `I` (Stacks 091S), then `K` is derived complete along the ideal sheaf
`I·\underline{Λ}` (Stacks 0999).

On an affine object `W` with w-contractible ring of global sections, derived sections carry
`T(K, l) = 0` for `l ∈ I` to `T(RΓ(W, K), l|_W) = 0`; the sections of `I·\underline{Λ}` over `W`
form the ideal generated by these `l|_W`, along which `RΓ(W, K)` is then derived complete. -/
theorem isDerivedComplete_of_isDerivedComplete_derivedModuleEquiv_inverse_obj (I : Ideal Λ)
    {K : DerivedSheaves.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ}
    (hK : IsDerivedComplete I ((derivedModuleEquiv.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ).inverse.obj K)) :
    RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u + 1, u, max (u + 1) w, w}
      (constantCoefficientRingedSite.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ)
      (constantCoefficientIdealSheaf.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ I) K := by
  have hI : I.FG := (isNoetherian_def.mp inferInstance) I
  refine (RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_iff_derivedSections_of_sliceTestingFamily.{u + 1, u, w}
    _ (Scheme.ProEt.testingFamily.{max (u + 1) w} X) _ K).2 fun W hW => ?_
  let Rs := Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
    (constantCoefficientRingedSite.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ).O
  let R := Rs.obj.obj (op W)
  let : IsMulCommutative R := by
    show IsMulCommutative ((constantCoefficientRingedSite.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ).O.obj.obj
      (op W))
    infer_instance
  let : CommRing R := inferInstance
  let F := SheafOfModules.evaluation.{max (u + 1) w} Rs (op W)
  let hAdd : F.Additive := Functor.additive_of_preserves_binary_products _
  let hColim : PreservesFiniteColimits F :=
    RingedSite.evaluation_preservesFiniteColimits_of_sliceTestingFamily Rs
      (Scheme.ProEt.testingFamily.{max (u + 1) w} X) W hW
  let : HasExactLimitsOfShape (Discrete ℕ) (ModuleCat.{max (u + 1) w} R) :=
    moduleCat_hasExactLimitsOfShape_discrete.{max (u + 1) w} R ℕ
  let hProd : HasProductsOfShape ℕ (DerivedCategory (ModuleCat.{max (u + 1) w} R)) :=
    Stacks.DerivedProducts.hasProductsOfShape_derivedCategory
  refine ⟨hAdd, inferInstance, hColim, hProd, fun f hf => ?_⟩
  let E := constantCoefficientModuleEquiv.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ
  let : E.functor.Additive := Functor.additive_of_preserves_binary_products _
  let G := E.functor ⋙ F
  let φ := coefficientSectionsMap.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ W
  let K' := (derivedModuleEquiv.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ).inverse.obj K
  let e : G.mapDerivedCategory.obj K' ≅ F.mapDerivedCategory.obj K :=
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.DerivedRestrictScalars.mapDerivedCategoryCompIso E.functor F).app K' ≪≫
      F.mapDerivedCategory.mapIso ((derivedModuleEquiv.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ).counitIso.app K)
  have hG : PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete ℕ) G.mapDerivedCategory :=
    Functor.preservesProducts_mapDerivedCategory ℕ G
  have hgen : ∀ l ∈ I, IsDerivedCompleteAt (F.mapDerivedCategory.obj K) (φ l) := fun l hl => by
    have hab : ∀ P, G.map (l • 𝟙 P) = φ l • 𝟙 (G.obj P) := fun P => by
      ext z
      exact constantCoefficientModuleEquiv_functor_map_smul_id_val_app X P l W z
    have hsmul : G.mapDerivedCategory.map (l • 𝟙 K') = φ l • 𝟙 (G.mapDerivedCategory.obj K') :=
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.DerivedRestrictScalars.mapDerivedCategory_map_smul_id G l (φ l)
        (fun Z => Stacks.SemilinearFunctor.map_smul_id_mapHomologicalComplex G l (φ l) hab _ Z) K'
    exact (RingedSite.isDerivedCompleteAt_iff_of_iso e (φ l)).1
      (isDerivedCompleteAt_map_of_smul_id G.mapDerivedCategory hsmul (hK l hl))
  have hle : I.map φ ≤ derivedCompleteIdeal (A := R) (F.mapDerivedCategory.obj K) :=
    Ideal.map_le_iff_le_comap.2 fun l hl => mem_derivedCompleteIdeal_iff.2 (hgen l hl)
  have hf' : f ∈ I.map φ := by rwa [← constantCoefficientIdealSheaf_obj_eq_map X Λ I W hW hI]
  exact mem_derivedCompleteIdeal_iff.1 (hle hf')

omit [IsNoetherianRing Λ] in
/-- **Inverse image is `Λ`-linear**: it carries multiplication by `l ∈ Λ` on a sheaf of
`Λ`-modules to multiplication by `l` on its inverse image. Its right adjoint, restriction along
base change, visibly does. -/
theorem proetaleModuleInverseImage_map_smul_id {Z Y : Scheme.{u}} (g : Z ⟶ Y)
    (P : Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology Y) (ModuleCat.{max (u + 1) w} Λ)) (l : Λ) :
    (proetaleModuleInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} g Λ).map (l • 𝟙 P) =
      l • 𝟙 ((proetaleModuleInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} g Λ).obj P) :=
  (proetaleModuleInverseImageAdjunction.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} Λ g).map_smul_id_of_map_smul_id
    (fun _ _ => rfl) P l

omit [IsNoetherianRing Λ] in
/-- **Inverse image along an immersion preserves derived completeness along `I`** of complexes
of sheaves of `Λ`-modules (Stacks 091S): it is exact and `Λ`-linear, and it commutes with
countable products (Stacks 09BU), which are exact for sheaves of modules on the pro-étale sites. -/
theorem isDerivedComplete_mapDerivedCategory_proetaleModuleInverseImage {Z Y : Scheme.{u}}
    (g : Z ⟶ Y) [IsImmersion g] (I : Ideal Λ)
    {K : DerivedCategory (Sheaf (Scheme.ProEt.topology Y) (ModuleCat.{max (u + 1) w} Λ))}
    (hK : IsDerivedComplete I K) :
    IsDerivedComplete I
      ((proetaleModuleInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} g Λ).mapDerivedCategory.obj K) := by
  let gΛ := proetaleModuleInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} g Λ
  have := preservesLimitsOfShape_proetaleModuleInverseImage_of_isImmersion.{w} Λ g (Discrete ℕ)
  have : PreservesLimitsOfShape (Discrete ℕ) gΛ.mapDerivedCategory :=
    Functor.preservesProducts_mapDerivedCategory ℕ gΛ
  exact fun l hl => isDerivedCompleteAt_map_of_smul_id gΛ.mapDerivedCategory
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.DerivedRestrictScalars.mapDerivedCategory_map_smul_id gΛ l l
      (fun M => Stacks.SemilinearFunctor.map_smul_id_mapHomologicalComplex gΛ l l
        (proetaleModuleInverseImage_map_smul_id g · l) _ M) K) (hK l hl)

/-- **Restriction to a locally closed subscheme preserves derived completeness.** Let
`g : Z ⟶ X` be an immersion and `K` an object of `D(X_proét, Λ)` derived complete along
`I·\underline{Λ}`. Then `K|_Z` is derived complete along `I·\underline{Λ}`.

Read through `AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.derivedModuleEquiv`, derived completeness along the
ideal sheaf is derived completeness along `I`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.isDerivedComplete_derivedModuleEquiv_inverse_obj` and its
converse), which inverse image along an immersion preserves. -/
theorem isDerivedComplete_derivedInverseImage {Z : Scheme.{u}} (g : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion g]
    (I : Ideal Λ) {K : DerivedSheaves.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ}
    (hK : RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u + 1, u, max (u + 1) w, w}
      (constantCoefficientRingedSite.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ)
      (constantCoefficientIdealSheaf.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ I) K) :
    RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete.{u + 1, u, max (u + 1) w, w}
      (constantCoefficientRingedSite.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} Z Λ)
      (constantCoefficientIdealSheaf.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} Z Λ I)
      ((derivedInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} g Λ).obj K) :=
  isDerivedComplete_of_isDerivedComplete_derivedModuleEquiv_inverse_obj Z I fun l hl =>
    (RingedSite.isDerivedCompleteAt_iff_of_iso
      ((derivedModuleEquiv.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} Z Λ).unitIso.app _) l).1
      (isDerivedComplete_mapDerivedCategory_proetaleModuleInverseImage g I
        (isDerivedComplete_derivedModuleEquiv_inverse_obj X I hK) l hl)

/-- The reduction of the restriction along an immersion of a constructible complex has finite Tor
dimension. -/
private theorem hasFiniteTorDimension_derivedReduction_derivedInverseImage [CompactSpace X]
    {Z : Scheme.{u}} (g : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion g] (I : Ideal Λ)
    {K : DerivedSheaves.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ}
    (hK : IsConstructibleViaDerivedReduction.{u, w} X Λ I K) :
    Stacks.ModuleSheaf.HasFiniteTorDimension.{max (u + 2) (w + 1), max (u + 1) w, u, u + 1}
      ((derivedReduction.{u, w} Z Λ I).obj
        ((derivedInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} g Λ).obj K)) := by
  obtain ⟨a, b, h⟩ := Stacks.ModuleSheaf.exists_hasTorAmplitude_of_locallyHasFiniteTorDimension
    Scheme.ProEt.isTerminal_mk_id Scheme.ProEt.exists_finite_coversTop_le _ hK.2.2
  exact ⟨a, b, hasTorAmplitude_derivedReduction_derivedInverseImage_of_isImmersion g Λ I h⟩

/-- **Restriction of a constructible complex to a locally closed subscheme on which the
reduction has locally constant cohomology is constructible.** Let `X` be a quasi-compact scheme,
`g : Z ⟶ X` an immersion and `K` an object of `D_cons(X, Λ)` (Stacks 09C1) such that the
restrictions to `Z` of the cohomology sheaves of `K ⊗_Λ^L \underline{Λ/I}` are locally constant
of finite type. Then `K|_Z` lies in `D_cons(Z, Λ)`.

* `K|_Z` is derived complete (`AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.isDerivedComplete_derivedInverseImage`);
* the cohomology sheaves of `K|_Z ⊗_Λ^L \underline{Λ/I}` are the restrictions of those of
  `K ⊗_Λ^L \underline{Λ/I}`, locally constant of finite type, hence constructible;
* `K ⊗_Λ^L \underline{Λ/I}` has Tor amplitude in some `[a, b]` as `X` is quasi-compact, hence so
  has `K|_Z ⊗_Λ^L \underline{Λ/I}`, which therefore locally has finite Tor dimension. -/
theorem isConstructibleDerivedSheaf_derivedInverseImage [CompactSpace X] {Z : Scheme.{u}}
    (g : Z ⟶ X) [IsImmersion g] (I : Ideal Λ) {K : DerivedSheaves.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ}
    (hK : IsConstructibleViaDerivedReduction.{u, w} X Λ I K)
    (hlc : ∀ i : ℤ, Stacks.ConstantSheaf.IsFiniteTypeLocallyConstantModuleSheaf.{u, u + 1,
        max (u + 1) w, max (u + 1) w} (Scheme.ProEt.topology Z) (Λ ⧸ I)
      ((proetaleModuleInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} g (Λ ⧸ I)).obj
        ((DerivedCategory.homologyFunctor _ i).obj ((derivedReduction.{u, w} X Λ I).obj K)))) :
    IsConstructibleViaDerivedReduction.{u, w} Z Λ I
      ((derivedInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} g Λ).obj K) := by
  refine ⟨isDerivedComplete_derivedInverseImage X g I hK.1, fun i => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_homology_derivedReduction_derivedInverseImage_iso g Λ I K i
    exact isConstructibleModuleSheaf'_of_isFiniteTypeLocallyConstant _
      (ObjectProperty.prop_of_iso _ e.symm (hlc i))
  · exact (hasFiniteTorDimension_derivedReduction_derivedInverseImage X g I
      hK).locallyHasFiniteTorDimension

/-- **Restriction of a constructible complex to an open subscheme is constructible.** Let `X` be
a quasi-compact scheme, `j : U ⟶ X` an open immersion and `K` an object of `D_cons(X, Λ)`. Then
`K|_U` lies in `D_cons(U, Λ)`: as for
`AlgebraicGeometry.ProEtale.isConstructibleDerivedSheaf_derivedInverseImage`, except that the
cohomology sheaves of the reduction stay constructible on restriction to an open subscheme. -/
theorem isConstructibleDerivedSheaf_derivedInverseImage_of_isOpenImmersion [CompactSpace X]
    {U : Scheme.{u}} (j : U ⟶ X) [IsOpenImmersion j] (I : Ideal Λ)
    {K : DerivedSheaves.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} X Λ}
    (hK : IsConstructibleViaDerivedReduction.{u, w} X Λ I K) :
    IsConstructibleViaDerivedReduction.{u, w} U Λ I
      ((derivedInverseImage.{u, max (u + 1) w, w} j Λ).obj K) := by
  refine ⟨isDerivedComplete_derivedInverseImage X j I hK.1, fun i => ?_, ?_⟩
  · obtain ⟨e⟩ := nonempty_homology_derivedReduction_derivedInverseImage_iso j Λ I K i
    exact ObjectProperty.prop_of_iso _ e.symm
      (isConstructibleModuleSheaf'_proetaleModuleInverseImage j _ (hK.2.1 i))
  · exact (hasFiniteTorDimension_derivedReduction_derivedInverseImage X j I
      hK).locallyHasFiniteTorDimension

